---json
{
  "layout": "layouts/base.njk",
  "title": "Privacy Policy",
  "permalink": "/privacy-policy/",
  "documentTitle": "Privacy Policy — Kate Courtright",
  "updated": "2026-11-07",
  "points": [
    "No cookies, no analytics, and no tracking scripts.",
    "No contact, newsletter or sign-up forms — this site doesn’t collect your name or email address.",
    "Fonts and images are served from this site, not from third-party services.",
    "Links to bookstores and social sites take you to services with their own privacy policies."
  ]
}
---
<main id="main" class="wrap">
  <article class="policy prose">
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="policy-updated">Last updated <time datetime="{{ updated }}">{{ updated | readableDate }}</time></p>

    <section class="policy-summary" aria-labelledby="policy-short">
      <h2 id="policy-short">The short version</h2>
      <ul class="policy-points">
        {% for point in points %}<li><svg width="16" height="16" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.4" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12l5 5L20 7"/></svg><span>{{ point }}</span></li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
    </section>

    <h2>Hosting</h2>
    <p>This site is hosted on GitHub Pages. GitHub logs visitors’ IP addresses for security purposes; Kate doesn’t have access to those logs. See <a href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub’s privacy statement</a>.</p>

    <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
    <p>Bookstores, social sites and share buttons linked from this site have their own privacy policies, and purchases are handled entirely by the retailer you choose. To unsubscribe from Kate’s newsletter, use the link in any newsletter email.</p>

    <p class="policy-questions">Questions? <a href="/contact/">Get in touch</a>.</p>
  </article>
</main>
